# IDOR in GET /invoices/:id

**Endpoint:** `GET /invoices/:id` (requires any valid session)

## Summary
`requireUser` authenticates the caller and stores `res.locals.userId`, but the
`/invoices/:id` handler never uses it. It selects the invoice by `id` alone, with no
`owner_id = res.locals.userId` condition. The list endpoint `GET /invoices` does filter by owner,
which shows that the single-invoice route is missing the check.

## Reproduction
1. Register an account and log in to get a bearer token.
2. Call `GET /invoices/1`, `GET /invoices/2`, ... with your own token.
3. Full invoice rows (`SELECT *`) belonging to other customers are returned.

## Impact
Any authenticated user can enumerate and read every other customer's invoices (amounts, status and
all other columns).

## Fix
Query `WHERE id = $1 AND owner_id = $2` with `res.locals.userId`, and return 404 otherwise."}],"response_format":{"type":"json_schema","json_schema":{"name":"verdict","strict":true,"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"valid":{"type":"boolean"},"severity":{"type":"string","enum":["none","low","medium","high","critical"]},"cwe":{"type":["string","null"]},"confidence":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":100}},"required":["valid","severity","cwe","confidence"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"chat_template_kwargs":{"enable_thinking":false},"temperature":0,"max_tokens":400}

